reccmp master: Replace stale containing global data

A corrected global can start inside a larger data item that an earlier sync
created from an incorrect source declaration. `getDataAt` does not return that
containing item, so `createData` fails and leaves the stale type in place.

Remove the data item that contains the new start address. The importer already
removes later data items from the new range. Together, these operations let the
current PDB declaration replace stale generated data in either direction.

Generated against reccmp commit e043de8b.
Apply from the reccmp submodule root with `patch -p1`.

diff --git a/reccmp/ghidra/importer/globals_importer.py b/reccmp/ghidra/importer/globals_importer.py
index d6bbc671..03bfac13 100644
--- a/reccmp/ghidra/importer/globals_importer.py
+++ b/reccmp/ghidra/importer/globals_importer.py
@@ -43,7 +43,10 @@ def import_global_into_ghidra(
         data_type = type_importer.import_pdb_type_into_ghidra(node.data_type.key)
         address_ghidra = api.getAddressFactory().getAddress(hex(glob.orig_addr))
 
-        existing_data = api.getDataAt(address_ghidra)
+        # A previous sync can leave a larger data item at an address that now
+        # belongs to a corrected, smaller global. Remove the containing item so
+        # the current PDB type can replace it.
+        existing_data = api.getDataContaining(address_ghidra)
         if existing_data is not None:
             api.removeData(existing_data)
 
